# toke — outstanding work register

Everything left incomplete against a plan acceptance criterion, or
claimed-but-unverified, across Phases 0–9 and the work since.

Maintained alongside [IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md](IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md). The plan
says what the phases are; this file says what they did not deliver. Add an
entry the moment something is skipped — a deferral that lives only in a commit
message is a deferral nobody will find.

Sections 1–6 are work. **Section 7 is not**: it holds choices that were
considered and declined, so they stop reading as debt and nobody rediscovers
them as problems.

Status: `OPEN` · `BLOCKED` (needs another task first) · `CLOSED` (with what
closed it) · `DONE`

Last audited: 2026-09-22, against the code at v0.2.0. Entries closed by later work are
marked CLOSED with what closed them; deliberate choices live in §7 rather than here.

---

## 1. Defects — introduced, not deferred

### DEF-1 · Grouped objects disappear from the canvas · DONE · 2026-09-21
`groupSelection` moves children into the group node, so they leave the
top-level array. `StudioCanvas.buildFabricObject` returns `null` for
`kind: 'group'`, and the render loop only walks top-level nodes — so the
children are never drawn.

The P3 e2e asserted the layers **tree** showed three items after grouping and
never checked the canvas, which is exactly how this got through.

**Fixed:** `renderableNodes` flattens groups to leaves in paint order — groups
hold absolute coordinates, so no transform stack is needed. Selecting a group
now selects every leaf inside it.

The viewport exposes `data-fabric-objects`, so browser tests can assert what
Fabric actually holds rather than what the tree claims. Two regression tests
cover place/undo and group/ungroup.

### DEF-2 · Canvas text edits may not reach the store · OPEN · medium
Double-clicking an `IText` enters Fabric's editor. `commitFromFabric` reads
`object.text` on `object:modified`, but Fabric emits `text:changed` and
`editing:exited` for text edits and it is unverified that `object:modified`
fires at all.

- **Accept:** double-click a text object, type, click away; the new string
  survives an undo/redo round trip and appears in the layers tree.

---

## 2. Blocked on a later phase

### BLK-1 · Image tool · CLOSED
The asset store is content-addressed, the PDF renderer embeds PNG/JPEG from
bytes handed to it on the export job, and the UI is built: a file input on the
toolbar (`ImageImport.tsx`), `FabricImage` construction from `objectUrlFor`,
retain wired to node creation, and asset bytes collected into `packProject`.

Verified end to end in `e2e/images.spec.ts`: place, resize, choose a fit mode,
export a PDF carrying one image XObject for the whole sheet, and reopen a
saved `.toke` with the image intact.

Two follow-ons remain open under their own entries — INC-34 (no crop
rectangle) and INC-35 (no aspect lock on resize).

### BLK-2 · Pen / path tool · OPEN (unblocked) · from P3.4
**Unblocked by P8.2** — `renderNode` now draws a `PathNode` via `drawSvgPath`.
`PathNode` and the Fabric mapping exist; the drawing interaction does not.
Large interaction (anchors, bezier handles).

### BLK-3 · Token-bound indicator in the layers tree · OPEN (unblocked) · from P3.10
**Unblocked by P6.** `isTokenised(node.text)` now answers this. `LayersPanel`
still hardcodes `const bound = false`; the inspector shows a bound badge but
the layer tree does not. Render the `--bound` colour **plus** a text label —
CLAUDE.md §4.7 forbids signalling state by colour alone.

### BLK-4 · Diagnostics panel wiring · CLOSED by P9.2 · from P2.1, P3
Errors currently surface as one-off `role="alert"` paragraphs. Every
`AppError` already carries `objectId`; nothing consumes it yet.

- **Accept:** every error reaches the diagnostics panel, and clicking one with
  an `objectId` selects that canvas object.

