## 3. Incomplete against a plan acceptance criterion

These were signed off as phase-complete with parts missing. Each names the
criterion it fails.

### INC-1 · Rulers · OPEN · P3.3
> "Rulers in the active display unit with a live cursor indicator. Ruler ticks
> stay legible from 10% to 1600% (adaptive subdivision)."

`CanvasRulers.tsx` was never written. Zoom, pan and fit all work; the rulers do
not exist.

### INC-2 · Guides cannot be created · OPEN · P3.7
The snapping engine is complete and tested, `guides` lives in the store and
`addGuide` exists — but nothing calls it. There is no drag-from-ruler
interaction (blocked by INC-1) and no guide rendering.

Also missing from the same criterion:
- **Snap indicators** — `snap()` returns `matches`; nothing draws them.
- **Ctrl suspends snapping** — only the toolbar checkbox toggles it.

### INC-3 · Pan by space-drag and middle-drag · OPEN · P3.3
> "space-drag and middle-drag pan"

Only wheel/trackpad pan is implemented.

### INC-4 · Layers panel is read-only · OPEN · P3.10
> "Reorder by drag, rename, toggle visibility/lock, select."

Only **select** is implemented. `visible` and `locked` exist on every node and
are honoured by the Fabric mapping, but there is no UI to change them.

### INC-5 · Data grid: column resize · OPEN · P2.6
> "Sort, column resize, inline cell edit, row add/delete."

Columns are fixed at 150px. Long values truncate with no way to widen.

### INC-6 · Data grid: no "add row" control · OPEN · P2.6
`useDataStore.addRow` exists and works. The button was on the old single-panel
page and was dropped when the studio shell replaced it in P3. Row deletion
survives only as Shift+Delete, which is undiscoverable.

### INC-7 · CSV column mapping is not editable · OPEN · P2.7
> "column mapping UI (source → target, or 'create column', or 'ignore') →
> type confirmation → import with progress"
> "Mapping is fully keyboard-operable. Inferred types are shown and
> overridable."

`proposeMapping` output is **displayed** in the preview header but cannot be
changed. A user whose CSV column is matched wrongly has no recourse but to
edit the file. Missing:
- per-column target selector (map / create / ignore)
- per-column type override
- import progress indicator

### INC-8 · Record source has no UI · CLOSED by P9.3
`runRecordSource` and `columnSchemaFor` were built and tested but called from
nowhere. The SQL console now drives them: `SqlConsole.tsx` runs any read-only
query and "Use as record source" hands it to `setRecordSource`.

### INC-9 · Align and distribute have no keyboard shortcuts · OPEN · P3.8
Toolbar buttons only. CLAUDE.md §4.7 commits to full keyboard operation.

### INC-10 · Nudge is not coalesced in history · OPEN · P3.9
> "A drag is one entry, not one per mousemove."

Fabric emits `object:modified` once per drag, so **drags are fine**. Held
arrow keys are not: each keypress pushes its own history entry, so nudging an
object ten steps costs ten undos. `coalesceKey` is implemented and tested in
the history module but no call site passes one.

- **Fix:** pass a `coalesceKey` such as `nudge:<selection-ids>` from
  `useCanvasStore.nudge`.

### INC-11 · Assets and fonts are not collected into a save · PARTLY CLOSED
Assets now travel inside the `.toke` and into the export job; a saved project
with an image reopens with the image. Fonts still do not: v1 ships one family
and bundles it, so carrying ~218KB per face in every project file would buy
nothing. Revisit with custom font upload.


### INC-13 · Multi-design projects cannot be created or switched · OPEN · P4.2
The format stores `designs` as an array and round-trips several, but
`toProject` always writes exactly one and `fromProject` reads only the first.
No UI to add, rename or switch designs.

### INC-14 · No BroadcastChannel single-writer lock · OPEN · P4.4
> "BroadcastChannel single-writer lock, crash-recovery prompt."

Recovery works. The lock does not exist: two tabs open on the same project
both autosave, and the last write wins silently.

### INC-15 · Only the bundled Plex faces load · OPEN · P5.1
`ensureFontsLoaded` fetches three hardcoded faces from `/fonts`. There is no
user font upload, no font picker, and `loadFont`'s TTF/OTF path is only
exercised by the WOFF fixture. The loader supports it; nothing calls it.

### INC-16 · Bundled fonts are WOFF, not TTF/OTF · DONE · 2026-09-22
**Fixed.** Switched to @expo-google-fonts, which ships TTF. Verified the
metrics are byte-identical to the WOFF first (zero delta across all three
faces), so the P5.3 agreement still holds — and now the SAME file is measured,
served to the browser and embedded in the PDF. @fontsource removed.


### INC-18 · Record source is still the raw guests table · DONE · 2026-09-21
**Fixed in P7.1.** `useDataStore` now holds `recordSource`, `records` and
`recordColumns` separately from the grid's table view, validated read-only on
the main thread before the query is sent. Live Mode and pre-flight both read
`records`.

Still open as INC-21: there is no UI to EDIT the record source, so it is
always the default `SELECT * FROM guests`.

### INC-19 · Overflow is not shown in the binding panel · OPEN · P6.6
The canvas draws a rust outline and pre-flight lists every affected record,
but the binding panel itself does not say the currently previewed record
overflows.

### INC-21 · No record-source editor · CLOSED by P9.3
The SQL console is the editor. A design can print only accepted guests by
running the filter and pressing "Use as record source"; the templates ship
with exactly that query. A simpler filter control on top of it remains
possible but is no longer blocking anything.

### INC-22 · Pre-flight does not check images or fonts · OPEN · P7.3
> "Report per-record: text overflow, unresolved tokens, missing assets."

Overflow, unresolved and empty are covered. Missing assets are not, because
image placement does not exist yet (BLK-1) — though the PDF renderer now
errors with `PDF_ASSET_MISSING` rather than exporting a hole, so the failure
is loud at export time even without a pre-flight check. A missing font face
is also unchecked: `getFont` returning null silently skips the fit check.

### INC-23 · Cover images overflow their frame in the PDF · CLOSED
The renderer now emits a clip path for cover-fit images, balanced with the
graphics state so it cannot leak into the next card on the sheet. The fit
maths moved to `engine/scene/image.ts`, which the canvas and the PDF renderer
both call — one definition of what 'cover' means.

### INC-24 · Export sends every registered font, not just the used faces · OPEN · P8.8
`fontsForExport` ships the whole registry across the worker boundary because
the worker has its own empty registry and a missing fallback face would fail
mid-render. Subsetting makes the embedded cost near-zero, but the postMessage
copy is ~218KB per face. Narrow to referenced faces once the scene records
which it uses.


### INC-26 · Export has no memory ceiling · OPEN · P8.8
The plan's budget is 500 records under 30s and under 1GB. The 30s half is
asserted in `assemble.golden.test.ts`; memory is not measured anywhere, and
the whole document is held in memory until `finish`. Streaming incremental
save is the fix if a run ever exceeds it.

### INC-27 · Proof export is not reachable from the UI · OPEN · P8.9
`exportProof` and the worker's `proof` op both exist and are tested, but
nothing in the shell calls them — the Export dialog only runs a full sheet
export. Needs a "Proof current record" action.

### INC-33 · Undo was a no-op for every inspector edit · CLOSED
The replacement command built its inverse lazily — `previous ??= document.nodes`
inside `invert()` — and `invert` is called at UNDO time, after `apply` has
already changed the state. It captured the new nodes and "restored" them, so
binding edits, align, distribute, reorder and group were undoable in name only.
Never caught, because the undo tests all used `addNode`/`deleteSelection`,
which compute their inverses from the node itself.

Fixed by deleting `invert` entirely: the history stack already snapshots the
state before every command, and a coalesced gesture's entry deliberately holds
the state from before the WHOLE gesture — which no per-command inverse can
reconstruct. Less code and correct for drags.

### INC-34 · Image crop is fit-mode only, no crop rectangle · KNOWN
Fit, Fill and Stretch against the frame, with the frame resizable. There is no
drag-a-crop-box-over-the-image interaction and no pan-within-frame. Adding one
means a `cropRect` on `ImageNode` and a `.toke` schemaVersion bump.

### INC-35 · Image resize does not lock aspect · OPEN
The frame resizes freely; with Fit or Fill the picture stays undistorted
inside it, but Stretch will distort and nothing warns. A Shift-drag aspect
lock on the canvas handles is the fix.


### INC-30 · Font weight 500 is not bundled · CLOSED
Worse than recorded. `getFont` fell back to the nearest loaded face, so
**fontkit measured Plex 400 while the browser's own CSS matching fell back to
a system font** — auto-fit passed against one typeface and the canvas drew
another, at roughly double the width. Caught by looking at a screenshot, not
by any test.

Fixed by bundling `plex-sans-500-normal.ttf`, with a fitness test asserting
that every weight the scene graph can ask for is actually shipped and that
each bundled URL resolves to a file in `public/`.

### INC-31 · Pre-flight does not check font availability · OPEN · P7.3, P9.4
`getFont` now substitutes the nearest weight instead of returning null, so a
missing face is silent rather than fatal. Pre-flight should report the
substitution before export, not after the cards are printed a weight lighter
than the proof.

### INC-32 · The e2e suite is contention-sensitive · KNOWN · P9.5
117 tests, two workers, each booting a SQLite WASM worker against one
Turbopack dev server. Timeouts were raised to 30s per assertion and 90s per
test to match the real work; a failure under load is still possible and CI
runs one worker with two retries. Not masked with blanket retries locally,
since that would hide genuine flakes.

### INC-20 · Token errors do not reach a diagnostics surface · CLOSED by P9.2
Resolution errors and auto-fit overflow now report to the diagnostics panel
with the offending objectId, which makes each finding click-to-focus. The
object still falls back to its template on canvas — a vanished object is
harder to diagnose than a wrong one — but the reason no longer disappears
with it.

---

## 4. Claimed but never verified

Acceptance criteria that were written into the plan and not actually
exercised. Each needs a test, not an opinion.

### VER-1 · Canvas mount/unmount leak · OPEN · P3.2
> "Mount/unmount 50 times without leaking listeners or canvases (assert
> listener count)."

Never run. React StrictMode double-mounts in dev, so a leak here is likely
already happening unnoticed.

### VER-2 · Data grid at 10,000 rows · OPEN · P2.6
> "10,000 rows scroll at 60fps."

Virtualisation is wired via `@tanstack/react-virtual` but was only ever
exercised with three rows.

### VER-3 · Multi-select resize origin · OPEN · P3.5
> "Multi-select resize scales all members proportionally about the correct
> origin."

Delegated entirely to Fabric's `ActiveSelection`; never asserted.

### VER-4 · Marquee selection · OPEN · P3.5
Fabric's default drag-select is enabled but untested.

### VER-7 · Measurement agreement on a non-bundled font · OPEN · P5.3
The 0.5pt agreement is proved for three Plex faces. A user-supplied TTF has
never been checked, and that is the case most likely to diverge.

### VER-6 · Autosave under a real storage quota · OPEN · P4.4
`onError` is tested with a thrown error, but a genuine `QuotaExceededError`
from a large project has never been produced. Worth a test that fills the
store.

### VER-5 · Numeric fields during a live drag · OPEN · P3.6
> "Values update live during canvas drag without fighting user input
> mid-edit."

Fields update on `object:modified` (drag end), not during the drag. The
"without fighting input" half is satisfied; the "live" half is not.

